Returned: {"epic":"jira:SYN-1","summary":"Checkout v2: phone wallets and saved cards","a":"new:1","b":"new:2"}
Captured 2 changes:
{"op":"createStory","target":null,"ref":"new:1","args":{"summary":"Placeholder story 1 (trial, to be removed)","description":"Temporary placeholder created to try out changes in Oriel. Not real work.","epic":"jira:SYN-1"}}
{"op":"createStory","target":null,"ref":"new:2","args":{"summary":"Placeholder story 2 (trial, to be removed)","description":"Temporary placeholder created to try out changes in Oriel. Not real work.","epic":"jira:SYN-1"}}
They become the change set the user reviews when this turn ends, unless a later run in this turn captures changes instead.
Once applied, the user may undo them with Revert in the thread, where the change set offers it, which proposes the reverse as a new change set.
Nothing is sent until the user approves: say you proposed them, never that they're done.

